   "html_text": "Given the plurality of truth-functionally complete sets of connectives, why would Frege or anyone else select the material conditional as a primitive connective for classical logic? Frege saw that the value of selecting the material conditional as a primitive connective not from its approximation of ordinary language expression but from its role internal to logical theory. Let us write ⟦M⟧ to indicate that the formula B is valid in the classical theory of truth. Generalizing this turnstile notat",
